# Drift guard for the DefaultReportImpl shadow.
#
# The DefaultReportImpl.java sitting next to this file is a SHADOW of
# EPUBCheck's own com.adobe.epubcheck.util.DefaultReportImpl: it is the
# upstream source copied verbatim, plus a doc comment and two small mirror
# blocks that call ecshim.ReportTap (this is how the live report-event tap
# works -- see agent-docs/CONTINUATION.md). The shims jar precedes the
# EPUBCheck jars on the TeaVM compiler classpath, so our copy wins.
#
# WHAT THIS GUARDS
# The line below is the sha256 of the PRISTINE upstream DefaultReportImpl.java
# (no tap blocks) for the EPUBCheck version the shadow was last ported from.
# At build time scripts/check-shadow-drift.ts pulls that same file out of the
# epubcheck-<version>-sources.jar and hashes it. If EPUBCheck changed the file
# in a version bump, the hashes differ and the build FAILS loudly -- otherwise
# our shadow would silently keep the OLD upstream behavior while pretending to
# be the new EPUBCheck.
#
# WHAT TO DO ON A MISMATCH
# 1. Diff the new upstream file against our shadow:
#      unzip -p build/epubcheck-<version>-sources.jar \
#        com/adobe/epubcheck/util/DefaultReportImpl.java > /tmp/upstream.java
#      diff /tmp/upstream.java \
#        teavm/shims/src-teavm/com/adobe/epubcheck/util/DefaultReportImpl.java
#    (our shadow only adds the doc comment and the two "ecshim.ReportTap" blocks;
#     any OTHER difference is a real upstream change.)
# 2. Re-port: start from the NEW upstream source and re-apply ONLY the two
#    mirror blocks (message() -> ReportTap.emitMessage, info() -> ReportTap.emitInfo)
#    plus the doc comment. Keep the rest byte-for-byte upstream.
# 3. Replace the shadow file with that re-ported version.
# 4. Update the hash line below to the new upstream file's sha256, e.g.:
#      unzip -p build/epubcheck-<version>-sources.jar \
#        com/adobe/epubcheck/util/DefaultReportImpl.java | shasum -a 256
#
# EPUBCheck version the hash below is for: 5.3.0
57e986cdddabb4d0221376574c16191da898079b0b0ca96e534466ab1197f378
